  "id": "jackiw_teitelboim_black_hole",
  "name": "Jackiw-Teitelboim Black Hole",
  "short_name": "Jackiw-Teitelboim",
  "description": "A black hole in two spacetime dimensions, in the gravity of Teitelboim and Jackiw, where a scalar field, the dilaton, holds the curvature at $R = -2/L^2$. Every solution is a piece of anti-de Sitter space of two dimensions, and the dilaton tells the black hole from empty space: its value on the horizon is the entropy. The same gravity governs the throat of a nearly extreme charged black hole, and in it the quantum mechanics of a black hole can be solved exactly.",
